course: dictionary
lesson: 4408
title: Medical words for everyday things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound grand because they come from doctors and health books. Halitosis is one of them. It is a long, formal word for bad breath, the kind of breath that smells unpleasant.
explain: «Halitosis» is the medical-sounding name for bad breath. The word medical is a clue: it belongs to the world of doctors and health. Everyday people usually say «bad breath» instead.
explain: Both words mean the same thing, but they feel different. One sounds like a doctor's notes and the other sounds like something a friend would say. Swap «bad breath» into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Halitosis means bad breath, the kind of breath that smells unpleasant.
fact: You can say that someone suffers from halitosis, or that something can cause halitosis.
fact: Brushing your teeth and tongue, flossing and drinking water can help prevent halitosis.
fact: Small, embarrassing things about the body often get soft or fancy names: «body odour» for a sweaty smell, «halitosis» for bad breath, and «unmentionables» for underwear.
exercise: «Halitosis» is the medical-sounding name for what? | A sore tooth | Sweaty feet | A runny nose | *Bad breath
exercise: Which everyday phrase means the same as halitosis? | A bad cold | A lost voice | *Bad breath | Sweaty palms
exercise: Which of these can help prevent halitosis? | Eating only sweets all day | Never drinking any water | Staying up late every night | *Brushing your teeth and tongue
test: In «body odour», «halitosis» and «unmentionables», what kind of names are these? | Names of towns | Names of sports teams | Names of famous doctors | *Fancy or polite names for small, embarrassing body things
test: Which sentence uses halitosis correctly? | *Mum says brushing and flossing can help stop halitosis | Halitosis is a colour of paint | My bike has a loud halitosis | I put halitosis in my sandwich
exam: What does this mean? «Halitosis» is the medical-sounding name for bad breath. | A type of toothpaste | A sore throat | *Bad breath | A bad cold
